#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:1
msgid "Debugging LLVM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:3
msgid ""
"This document is a collection of tips and tricks for debugging LLVM using a "
"source-level debugger. The assumption is that you are trying to figure out "
"the root cause of a miscompilation in the program that you are compiling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:8
msgid "Extract and rerun the compile command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:10
msgid ""
"Extract the Clang command that produces the buggy code. The way to do this "
"depends on the build system used by your program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:13
msgid ""
"For Ninja-based build systems, you can pass `-t commands` to Ninja and "
"filter the output by the targeted source file name. For example: `ninja -t "
"commands myprogram | grep path/to/file.cpp`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:17
msgid ""
"For Bazel-based build systems using Bazel 9 or newer, you can pass `--"
"output=commands` to the `bazel aquery` subcommand for a similar result. For "
"example: `bazel aquery --output=commands 'deps(//myprogram)' | grep path/to/"
"file.cpp`. Build commands must generally be run from a subdirectory of the "
"source directory named `bazel-$PROJECTNAME`. Bazel typically makes the "
"target paths of `-o` and `-MF` read-only when running commands outside of a "
"build, so it may be necessary to change or remove these flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:26
msgid ""
"A method that should work with any build system is to build your program "
"under [Bear] and look for the compile command in the resulting "
"`compile_commands.json` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:30
msgid ""
"Once you have the command you can use the following steps to debug it. Note "
"that any flags mentioned later in this document are LLVM flags so they must "
"be prefixed with `-mllvm` when passed to the Clang driver, e.g. `-mllvm -"
"print-after-all`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:35
msgid "Understanding the source of the issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:37
msgid ""
"If you have a miscompilation introduced by a pass, it is frequently possible "
"to identify the pass where things go wrong by searching a pass-by-pass "
"printout. The following options control when IR is printed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:42
msgid ""
"`-print-before-all` and `-print-after-all` print IR before or after every "
"pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:44
msgid ""
"`-print-before=<pass-name>` and `-print-after=<pass-name>` print IR around "
"selected passes. Multiple pass names can be separated by commas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:46
msgid ""
"`-print-pass-numbers` prints the pass names and their ordinals. `-print-"
"before-pass-number=<number>` and `-print-after-pass-number=<number>` can "
"then select particular pass invocations. Multiple numbers can be separated "
"by commas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:50
msgid ""
"`-print-changed` prints IR only after passes that change it. Its optional "
"modes include `quiet`, `diff`, `diff-quiet`, `cdiff`, `cdiff-quiet`, `dot-"
"cfg`, and `dot-cfg-quiet`. `-print-before-changed` also prints the IR before "
"each detected change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:55
msgid "The following options reduce or organize the output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:57
msgid ""
"`-filter-print-funcs=<function-name>` limits output to the listed functions. "
"Multiple names can be separated by commas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:59
msgid ""
"`-filter-print-source-locs=<file>:<line-list>` limits output to IR units "
"that contain a matching debug location. A line list can contain individual "
"lines and inclusive ranges, for example `-filter-print-source-locs=example."
"cpp:12,20-25`. The file may be a basename, a complete path, or a path "
"suffix. Inlined locations are also considered. Repeat the option to select "
"locations from more than one file. This option requires debug information, "
"such as that produced by Clang's `-g` option. It selects whole functions, "
"loops, or other IR units containing a match; it does not remove individual "
"nonmatching instructions from them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:68
msgid ""
"`-filter-passes=<pass-name>` limits `-print-changed` output to the listed "
"passes. Multiple names can be separated by commas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:70
msgid ""
"`-print-module-scope` prints the whole module instead of the IR unit on "
"which a pass runs. `-print-loop-func-scope` prints the containing function "
"for loop passes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:73
msgid ""
"`-ir-dump-directory=<directory>` writes `-print-before` and `-print-after` "
"output to files instead of standard error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:76
msgid ""
"For example, the following command prints the IR after every pass, but only "
"for functions containing instructions associated with the selected source "
"lines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:84
msgid ""
"By default, dumps are written to standard error. Pipe standard error into "
"`less` (append `2>&1 | less` to the command line) and use text search to "
"move between passes (for example, type `/Dump After<Enter>`, `n` to move to "
"the next pass, and `N` to move to the previous pass)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:89
msgid ""
"Metadata IDs remain stable across repeated pass and debug dumps, which makes "
"nodes easier to follow between snapshots. These IDs may contain gaps or "
"appear in a different order from normal complete-module LLVM IR output, "
"where metadata IDs are renumbered into a contiguous canonical sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:94
msgid ""
"You can sometimes pass `-debug` to get useful details about what passes are "
"doing. See also [PrintPasses.cpp] for the option definitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:97
msgid "Creating a debug build of LLVM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:99
msgid ""
"The subsequent debugging steps require a debug build of LLVM. Pass the `-"
"DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug` to CMake in a separate build tree to create a debug "
"build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:103
msgid "Understanding where an instruction came from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:105
msgid ""
"A common debugging task involves understanding which part of the code "
"introduced a buggy instruction. The pass-by-pass dump is sometimes enough, "
"but for complex or unfamiliar passes, more information is often required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:109
msgid ""
"The first step is to record a run of the debug build of Clang under [rr] "
"passing the LLVM flag `-print-inst-addrs` together with `-print-after-all` "
"and any desired filters. This will cause each instruction printed by LLVM to "
"be suffixed with a comment showing the address of the `Instruction` object. "
"You can then replay the run of Clang with `rr replay`. Because `rr` is "
"deterministic, the instruction will receive the same address during the "
"replay, so you can break on the instruction's construction using a "
"conditional breakpoint that checks for the address printed by LLVM, with "
"commands such as the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:124
msgid ""
"When the breakpoint is hit, you will likely be at the location where the "
"instruction was created, so you can unwind the stack with `bt` to see the "
"stack trace. It is also possible that an instruction was created multiple "
"times at the same address, so you may need to continue until reaching the "
"desired location, but in the author's experience this is unlikely to occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:131
msgid ""
"Similar flags exist for the backend: `-print-sdnode-addrs` for printing "
"`SDNode` addresses, and `-print-mi-addrs` for printing `MachineInstr` "
"addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:135
msgid "Identifying the source locations of instructions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DebuggingLLVM.md:137
msgid ""
"To identify the source location that caused a particular instruction to be "
"created, you can pass the LLVM flag `-print-inst-debug-locs` and each "
"instruction printed by LLVM is suffixed with the file and line number of the "
"instruction according to the debug information. Note that this requires "
"debug information to be enabled (e.g. pass `-g` to Clang)."
msgstr ""

